                                                                                                                                                    [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 200 +[38;2;248;248;242m  before the cascade runs. An atomic block over the ceiling becomes its own                                                                                                                                                                 [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 201 +[38;2;248;248;242m  oversized chunk and is flagged `is_atomic` — correctness beats the budget.                                                                                                                                                                [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 202 +[38;2;248;248;242m  19 chunks land here.                                                                                                                                                                                                                      [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 203 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **Budget:** TARGET 1 600 chars, CEILING 4 000.                                                                                                                                                                                            [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 204 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **Floor:** 320 chars. A trailing scrap below it merges into the chunk above;                                                                                                                                                              [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 205 +[38;2;248;248;242m  it's a fragment of that section, not a unit of its own.                                                                                                                                                                                   [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 206 +[38;2;248;248;242m- **Overlap:** none. Every chunk is prefixed at embed time with                                                                                                                                                                             [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 207 +[38;2;248;248;242m  `{title} > {label}`. Overlap buys context by duplicating tokens into the                                                                                                                                                                  [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 208 +[38;2;248;248;242m  index; a breadcrumb buys the same context for ~15 tokens and doesn't.                                                                                                                                                                     [5C[1B[49m[2m 209 [22m [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m[48;2;61;1;0m 201 -[38;2;248;248;242m- **Atomic blocks, never split:** fenced code, tables, a `Input:`/`Output:`                                                                                                                                                                 [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 202 -[38;2;248;248;242m  pair, a list whose items are one logical enumeration, any paragraph                                                                                                                                                                       [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 203 -[38;2;248;248;242m  containing a slot together with the paragraph that defines it.                                                                                                                                                                            [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 204 -[38;2;248;248;242m- **Budget:** 300–800 tokens target, 1 200 hard ceiling. An atomic block over                                                                                                                                                               [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 205 -[38;2;248;248;242m  the ceiling becomes its own oversized chunk — correctness beats the budget.                                                                                                                                                               [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 206 -[38;2;248;248;242m- **Floor:** chunks under 80 tokens merge into the previous sibling. Heading                                                                                                                                                                [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 207 -[38;2;248;248;242m  stubs shouldn't be retrievable units.                                                                                                                                                                                                     [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 208 -[38;2;248;248;242m- **Overlap:** none between siblings. Instead, every chunk is prefixed at embed                                                                                                                                                             [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 209 -[38;2;248;248;242m  time with `{prompt title} > {heading path}`. Overlap buys context by                                                                                                                                                                      [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 210 -[38;2;248;248;242m  duplicating tokens; a heading breadcrumb buys the same context for ~15 tokens                                                                                                                                                             [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 211 -[38;2;248;248;242m  and doesn't inflate the index.                                                                                                                                                                                                            [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 210 +[38;2;248;248;242mThe breadcrumb also earns its keep at rollup time — `label` is extracted from                                                                                                                                                               [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 211 +[38;2;248;248;242mwhichever delimiter made the cut, so the top labels across the corpus come out                                                                                                                                                              [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 212 +[38;2;248;248;242mas `instructions` (527), `guardrails` (112), `output` (91).                                                                                                                                                                                 [5C[1B[49m[2m 213 [22m [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m[48;2;61;1;0m 213 -[38;2;248;248;242mOn this corpus: ~60% of prompts (the 374 under 1 500 chars, plus part of the                                                                                                                                                                [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 214 -[38;2;248;248;242mnext bucket) become a single chunk equal to the whole prompt. Chunking only                                                                                                                                                                 [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 215 -[38;2;248;248;242mactually splits the tail — which is precisely the 276 currently being                                                                                                                                                                       [5C[1B[38;2;220;90;90m 216 -[38;2;248;248;242mtruncated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  [