                                                                                         [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 566 +[38;2;248;248;242m  cost worth paying for the truncation.                                                                                                                                                                                                     [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 567 +[38;2;248;248;242m- Set `RERANKER_DEVICE=cuda`. It defaults to `"cpu"` (`reranker.py:145`) on a                                                                                                                                                               [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 568 +[38;2;248;248;242m  two-3090 box. Same 50 pairs: **27 354 ms on CPU vs 249 ms on GPU.**                                                                                                                                                                       [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 569 +[38;2;248;248;242m- Consequence for §2: the reranker is **not** the binding constraint on chunk                                                                                                                                                               [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 570 +[38;2;248;248;242m  size. Sizing is governed by embedding dilution, which is flat to ~6 000                                                                                                                                                                   [5C[1B[38;2;80;200;80m 571 +[38;2;248;248;242m  chars, so TARGET 1 600 stands and there is no reason to drop it to 1 200.                                                                                                                                                                 [5C[1B[49m[2m 572 [22m [5C[1B[2m 573 [22m Corpus size doesn't argue against reranking here — 916 prompts is small, but[5C[1B[2m 574 [22m reranking runs over ~50 candidates r