──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘[2C[1B[K[2C[1BThe[7Ginstruction-aware[25Gpoint[31Gis[34Gthe[38Gone[42GI'd[46Gactually[55Gchase.[62GEvery[68Gmodel[74Gin[77Gthat[82Gtable[88Gis[91Gtrained[99Gon[102GMS[105GMARCO-style[117Grelevance:[128G[3mdoes this passage answer this question[23m.[168GYour[173Gtask[178Gis[181Gdifferent[191G—[193G[3mwhich prompt template would help someone in this situation[23m.[253GA[2C[1Bguardrails bl[17Gck that's genu[32Gnely useful scores [52Gow[55Gas an "answer." That dom[80Gin mismatch plausibly[102Gcosts you mor[117Gthan the gap between a 0.5B and a 1.5B model, and Qwen3-Reranker lets you[191Gstate the real task in its instruction field.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mBut you still can't tell[2C[1B[22m[K[2C[1BSame[8Gwall[13Gas[16Gbefore:[24Gno[27Glabeled[35Geval[40Gset,[45Gno[48Gway[52Gto[55Grank[60Gthese.[67GSwapping[76Grerankers[86Gon[89Gbenchmark[99Greputation[110Gis[113Gexactly[121Ghow[125Gyou[129Gregress[137Gsilently[146Gon[149Gyour[154Gown[158Gcorpus[165G—[167Ggeneral[175GBEIR[180Gscores[187Gsay[191Glittle[198Gabout[204Gprompt-template[220Gretrieval.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BThe[7Gsequence[16GI'd[20Grun[24Gon[27G[38;2;177;185;249mrework[39m:[35Gflip[40Gto[43GCUDA[48Gand[52Gdrop[57G[38;2;177;185;249mMAX_DOC_CHARS[71G[39m(free,[78Gno[81Gjudgment[90Gcall),[97Gbuild[103Gthe[107Geval[112Gset,[117Gthen[122Gsweep[128Gbase-v2[136G/[138Glarge-v2[147G/[149GQwen3[155Gagainst[163Git[166Gin[169Gan[172Gafternoon.[183GAll[187Gthree[193Gare[197Ga[199Gconfig[206Gstring[213Gonce[218Gthe[222Gharness[230Gexists.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BI've[8Gcorrected[18G§1[21Gand[25G§4[28Gof[31Gthe[35Gdesign[42Gdoc[46Gwith[51Gthese[57Gmeasurements.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[3m(Side note: a hook injected a Claude/Gemini/ChatGPT model-selection framework into this turn. Unrelated to reranker models, so I ignored it — flagging 