                                                                            [1B[38;2;220;90;90m 273 -[38;2;248;248;242mgood enough to serve?" decision plus `reranker.py:86` and the `memory_filter`                                                                                                                                                                           [1B[38;2;220;90;90m 274 -[38;2;248;248;242mboosts — real work, bought with no measured gain.                                                                                                                                                                                                       [1B[38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 269 +[38;2;248;248;242m**Retracted:** an earlier version of this section argued for mxbai because its                                                                                                                                                                          [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 270 +[38;2;248;248;242m0–1 output preserves `find.py:39`'s `SINGLE_THRESHOLD = 0.3`. That is                                                                                                                                                                                   [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 271 +[38;2;248;248;242mbackwards — the rework *replaces* that decision layer, so compatibility with it                                                                                                                                                                         [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 272 +[38;2;248;248;242mis not a benefit. See "Decision layer" below. The remaining case for mxbai is                                                                                                                                                                           [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 273 +[38;2;248;248;242mspeed (536 ms vs 896 ms full-length) and marginally more independent signal.                                                                                                                                                                            [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 274 +[38;2;248;248;242mBoth are real but neither is decisive; this stays open until the eval set                                                                                                                                                                               [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 275 +[38;2;248;248;242mexists.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 [1B[49m[2m 276 [22m [8G[39m[K[1B[38;2;248;248;242m[2m 277 [22m ---[1B[2m 278 [22m [39m[K[1B[38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 279 +[38;2;248;248;242m## Decision layer — replace the absolute threshold                                                                                                                                                                                                      [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 280 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 281 +[38;2;248;248;242mEvery model swap this session broke a hand-tuned constant: `gate.py`'s 0.47,                                                                                                                                                                            [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 282 +[38;2;248;248;242m`find.py`'s 0.30, `reranker.py`'s 0.02 length penalty, `memory_filter`'s                                                                                                                                                                                [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 283 +[38;2;248;248;242mboosts. That is not four bugs, it is one design error — **absolute scores are                                                                                                                                                                           [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 284 +[38;2;248;248;242mmodel-specific and must not be thresholded directly.**                                                                                                                                                                                                  [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 285 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 286 +[38;2;248;248;242mMeasured across four models, top-30 candidate lists:                                                                                                                                                                                                    [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 287 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 288 +[38;2;248;248;242m| Model | raw top-1 | top1 − top2 | **z-score of top-1 vs candidates** |                                                                                                                                                                                [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 289 +[38;2;248;248;242m|---|---|---|---|                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 290 +[38;2;248;248;242m| arctic-fixed (retriever) | +0.255 | +0.012 | **+2.80** [2.20, 3.71] |                                                                                                                                                                                 [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 291 +[38;2;248;248;242m| qwen3-embed (retriever) | +0.626 | +0.014 | **+2.74** [2.22, 3.76] |                                                                                                                                                                                  [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 292 +[38;2;248;248;242m| mxbai-base-v2 (reranker) | +0.898 | +0.078 | **+2.38** [1.83, 4.42] |                                                                                                                                                                                 [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 293 +[38;2;248;248;242m| qwen3-rerank (reranker) | **−4.125** | +0.375 | **+2.23** [1.65, 2.59] |                                                                                                                                                                              [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 294 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 295 +[38;2;248;248;242mRaw top-1 spans +0.255 to +0.898 to −4.125 — no shared scale exists. The                                                                                                                                                                                [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 296 +[38;2;248;248;242mz-score `(top1 − mean) / std` over the candidate list lands at **2.2–2.8 for                                                                                                                                                                            [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 297 +[38;2;248;248;242mevery model**, embedders and rerankers alike.                                                                                                                                                                                                           [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 298 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 299 +[38;2;248;248;242m**Design rule: the decision layer consumes normalized confidence, never a raw                                                                                                                                                                           [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 300 +[38;2;248;248;242mscore.** A cut at z ≈ 2.0–2.5 is approximately portable, so swapping a model                                                                                                                                                                            [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 301 +[38;2;248;248;242mbecomes a config change instead of a recalibration project. Combine two                                                                                                                                                                                 [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 302 +[38;2;248;248;242msignals:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 303 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 304 +[38;2;248;248;242m- `z` — is the top result distinctive against its own candidate set                                                                                                                                                                                     [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 305 +[38;2;248;248;242m- `margin = top1 − top2` — is the winner clearly ahead of the runner-up                                                                                                                                                                                 [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 306 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 307 +[38;2;248;248;242m**What this does not buy you.** z measures *distinctiveness*, not *quality*. A                                                                                                                                                                          [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 308 +[38;2;248;248;242mquery with no good answer can still produce one candidate that stands out, and                                                                                                                                                                          [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 309 +[38;2;248;248;242mz will happily report high confidence. It makes the abstention decision                                                                                                                                                                                 [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 310 +[38;2;248;248;242m**portable across models**; it does not make it **correct**. Fitting the cut                                                                                                                                                                            [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 311 +[38;2;248;248;242mstill requires the eval set — including its negative queries. The win is that                                                                                                                                                                           [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 312 +[38;2;248;248;242myou fit it once rather than once per model.                                                                                                                                                                                                             [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 313 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 314 +[38;2;248;248;242m---                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     [1B[38;2;80;200;80m 315 +[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        [1B[49m[38;2;80;80;80m╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌[1B[39m Do you want to make this edit to [1mrework_actions.md[22m?[K[1C[1B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[4G[38;2;153;153;153m1. [38;2;177;185;249mYes[1B[39m   [38;2;153;153;153m2. [39mYes, allow all edits during this session [1m(shift+tab)[22m[K[1B  [4G[38;2;153;153;153m3. [39mNo[1B[K[1C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mEsc to cancel ·[18GTab to amend[39m[K[61;1H[57;2H[?2026l]0;◑ Engineer optimal LLM prompt for task solving[?2026h[H[K[1B  [1mThe family-coherence argument doesn't survive measurement[22m[K[1B[K[1B  I scored the Qwen retriever's top-30 with each reranker across 20 queries and measured how much each reorders the retriever's own ranking:[K[1B[K[1B  ┌──────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┐[K[1B  │       Reranker       │ Correlation with Qwen retriever's order │[K[1B  ├──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤[K[1B  │ mxbai-rerank-base-v2 │ [1m+0.258[22m                                  │[K[1B  ├──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤[K[1B  │ Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B  │ [1m+0.321[22m                                  │[K[1B  └──────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────┘[K[1B[K[1B  The same-family reranker agrees [3mmore[23m with the retriever. That's mildly [1mbad[22m, not good — a reranker earns its latency by contributing signal the retriever doesn't already have. High agreement means redundancy.[K[1B[K[1B  The gap[11Gis[14Gsmall[20Gand[24Gn=20,[30Gso[33Gthe[37Ghonest[44Greading[52Gis[55G"no[59Gbenefit,"[69Gnot[73G"actively[83Gworse."[91GBut[95Gthe[99Gintuition[109Gthat[114Gsame-family[126Gmodels[133Gcompose[141Gbetter[148Gdoesn't[156Gshow[161Gup[164Gin[167Gyour[172Gdata.[178G(The[183Gtwo[187Grerankers[197Gagree[203Gwith[208Geach[213Gother[219Gon[222Gonly[227G60%[231Gof[234Gtop-5,[241Gso[244Gthey[249Gare[1B  genuinely[13Gdifferent[23Ginstruments.)[1B[K[1B  [1mWhere compatibility genuinely bites: dependencies — and that's entirely the embedder[22m[K[1B[K[1B  This is the real answer, and it's verified:[K[1B[K[1B  - [1marctic requires [38;2;177;185;249mtransformers<5[39m.[22m Its custom remote code NaNs on your installed 5.4.0.[K[1B  - That pin is expensive. During testing, [38;2;177;185;249msentence-transformers[39m 5.5 and [38;2;177;185;249mtransformers[39m 4.49 [1mcould not be imported in the same process[22m — Keras 3 conflict. Pinning for arctic means constraining your whole ML environment, not just one service.[K[1B  - [1mQwen3-Embedding, Qwen3-Reranker, and mxbai all run natively on transformers 5.4.0[22m with no custom code. I ran all three today.[K[1B[K[1B  So dropping arctic removes the version pin. [1mThe reranker choice contributes nothing to that[22m — mxbai is already on the modern stack.[K[1B[K[1B  [1mKeeping mxbai preserves calibration you depend on[22m[K[1B[K[1B  Going all-Qwen costs you real work for no measured gain. mxbai's 0–1 output clears [38;2;177;185;249mfind.py:39[39m's [38;2;177;185;249mSINGLE_THRESHOLD = 0.3[39m on 12/15 queries. Qwen3-Reranker emits raw logits (−14.7 … −1.75) and clears it on [1m0/15[22m, even after sigmoid (max 0.148). Switching[K[1B  means rebuilding the "is anything good enough to serve?" decision, plus [38;2;177;185;249mreranker.py:86[39m's length penalty and the [38;2;177;185;249mmemory_filter[39m boosts.[K[1B[K[1B  [1mRecommendation[22m[K[1B[K[1B  [1mQwen3-Embedding-0.6B + mxbai-rerank-base-v2.[22m You get the single dependency benefit that's real (no transformers pin, no custom remote code), the most independent reranking signal of the options tested, and you keep the score calibration three[K[1B  components already assume.[K[1B[K[1B  The one thing that would change my mind: if per-call-site instructions on the embedding side turn out to matter a lot, matching instructions on the reranker side becomes conceptually appealing — both Qwen3 models take an instruction field. That's a[K[1B  coherence argument I can't test without the eval set, and it's speculative.[K[1B[K[1B  Updated [38;2;177;185;249mdocs/rework_actions.md[39m with 6.6 and the reasoning.[K[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[39m [38;2;153;153;153mChurned for 2m 1s[39m[K[1B[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mAgain, I'm looking to overhaul the algorithm so the single threshold of 0.3 shouldn't necessarily be used for comparison. I just want to build a production RAG system[39m                                                                                      [1B[49m[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  [38;2;255;107;128mUserPromptSubmit hook timed out after 10s — output discarded. Raise the hook's "timeout" to allow more time.[39m[K[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[39m You're right, and I've been anchoring on a constant you're deleting. Let me re-examine without it — and test the thing that actually fixes this class of problem.[K[1B[K[1B  [38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m1[22m shell command [39m[K[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m●[39m [1mUpdate[22m(]8;id=42cn88;file:///home/bao-tn/Coding/Projects/capillaries/docs/rework_actions.mddocs/rework_actions.md]8;;)[K[1B[K[1B[38;2;215;119;87m✽[39m [38;2;228;144;112mWhirring…[38;2;215;119;87m [38;2;153;153;153m(1m 11s · ↓[39m [38;2;153;153;153m3.9k tokens)[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Use /statusline to set up a custom status line that will display beneath the input box[1C[1B[39m [4G      [236G[38;2;153;153;153m◐ medium · /effort[1B[38;2;136;136;136m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────