G     [64G      [4C[2B50/50[11Gfusion ([21Gday)[28GLexical collisions win — m[55Gasured, 4/4 real failures[4C[2B85/15 fusion    [28GInert; can't surface anything dense missed[2C[1B├[26G┼[81G┤[2C[1B│[5GRoute[11Gby[14Gspec[19Gtokens[26G│[28GFires[34Gon[37G19%,[42Gbut[46Gthe[50Gfilter[57Gis[60Gempty[66G93%[70Gof[73Gthose[81G│[2C[1B├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤[K[2C[1B│ [1mFilter-then-rank[22m     │[28G[1mDeletes the candidate set 93% of the time[81G[22m│[2C[1B└──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘[2C[1B[K[2C[1BTher[8G is one job spar[25Ge g[29Gnuinely[37Gdoes wel[46G here, and your golden set[73Gis[76Gthe[80Gevidence:[90G[1mname lookup.[103G[22mQueries[111Glike[116G[3m"build a 13-week cash flow model"[150G[23m→[152G[38;2;177;185;249m13-Week Cash Flow Model[176G[39mare[180Gtitle[186Gmatches,[195Gand[199Gsparse[206Ggot[210G17/20[216Gon[219Gexactly[227Gthat.[233GThat's[240Ga[242Greal[247Grole[252G—[2C[1Bthe[7Guser[12Gnaming[19Ga[21Gprompt[28Gthey[33Galready[41Gknow[46Gexists.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BSo[6Gthe[10Gnarrow,[18Gdefensible[29Gversion:[38G[1mrun sparse against titles and slugs only, not full chunk text.[101G[22mHigh[106Gprecision,[117Gno[120Gcollision[130Gsurface[138G(a[141Gtitle[147Gfield[153Gcan't[159Gaccidentally[172Gcontain[180G"budget"[189Gin[192Gan[195Gunrelated[205Gsense[211Gthe[215Gway[219Ga[221G1[223G700-char[232Gchunk[238Gcan),[244Gand[248Git[1B [3Gserves the one query[24Gshape[30Gsparse[37Gverifiably[48Ghandles[56Gon[59Gyour[64Gdata.[2B  I'd hold off on implementing that until you've labelled some of [38;2;177;185;249meval/plexus_queries.jsonl[39m — I've now been wrong twice about sparse by reasoning from unrepresentative evidence, and I'd rather the third answer come from labels.[K[2B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCogita