,[72Gtuning[79G[38;2;177;185;249mk[81G[39m—[83Ghas[87Gbeen[92Gfighting[101Gover[106G0.4[110Gpercentage[121Gpoints.[129GThe[133Gfusion[140Gstep[145Gis[148Gnot[152Gyour[157Gbottleneck[168Gand[172Gnever[178Gwas.[183GIt[186Greaches[194Gwithin[201Ga[203Grounding[212Gerror[218Gof[221Gits[225Gown[229Gtheoretical[241Gmaximum.[61;1H[59;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2;56r[4S[r[H[3GIt's[8Gnot[12Gan[15Galgorithm[25G—[27Git's[32Gan[35G[1mupper bound[22m.[48GThe[52Gquestion[61Git[64Ganswers[72Gis:[76G[3mif the merge step never made a single ordering mistake, how often would the right prompt land in the top 10?[2C[52B[23mThe[7Greason[14Git[17Gdoes[22Gso[25Gwell:[31Gyour[36Gcandidate[46Gpools[52G(50[56Gper[60Gchannel)[69Gare[73Gfive[78Gtimes[84Gthe[88Goutput[95Gsize[100G(10),[106Gso[109Gthe[113Gmerge[119Grarely[126Ghas[130Gto[133Gsacrifice[143Ga[145Ggenuine[153Ghit[157Gto[160Gmake[165Groom.[171GFusion[178Gonly[183Gloses[189Gwhen[194Gthe[198Glists[204Gare[208Gthe[212Gsame[217Glength[224Gas[227Gthe[231Goutput.[2C[2B[1mWhat this actually redirects you toward[22m[61;1H[59;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2;56r[2S[r[H[3GAnswer for your describing queries: 25.7%. That's the union — every prompt either channel found. No merge strategy can beat it, because fusion can only reorder what the channels already[189Gretrieved.[200GIt[203Gcan't[209Ginvent[216Ga[218Gdocument[227Gneither[235Gone[239Gfound.[2C[54BThe[7Gunion[13Gis[16G25.7%.[23GBoth[28Gchannels[37Gtogether[46Gmiss[51Gthree[57Gof[60Gevery[66Gfour[71Ganswers.[80GThat[85Ggap[89Gis[92Gin[95G[1mretrieval[22m,[106Gnot[110Gfusion[117G—[119Gand[123Git's[128G~25[132Gpoints[139Gwide[144Gversus[151G0.4.[61;1H[59;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2;56r[3S[r[H[3G[K[2C[53BThe[7Glevers[14Gthat[19Gcould[25Gmove[30Git,[34Groughly[42Gin[45Gorder[51Gof[54Gexpected[63Gvalue