[16Gis[19Gthe[23Gstrongest[33Gsingle[40Gchannel[48Gon[51Gevery[57Gbenchmark[67Gyou[71Ghave.[77GThe[81Gexact[87Gchannel[95Gis[98Gworth[104Gkeeping[112Gin[115Gthe[119Gcodebase[128Gas[131Ga[133Gstandalone[144Gtool[149G—[151G[38;2;177;185;249mpython3 -m capillaries.search.channels exact "serve.py"[207G[39m—[209Gfor[213Gthe[217Gday[221Gyou[225Ggenuinely[235Gneed[240Gto[243Gfind[248Ga[2C[1Bliteral string,[19Gbut[23Gi[25G should[33Gnot sit in the[48Gdefault retriev[64Gl path, because it can't [91Gswer the queri[106Gs your users[119Gactually[128Gtype.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BNothing[11Gin[14Gthe[18Gexisting[27Gpipeline[36Gchanged.[45G[38;2;177;185;249mretriever.py[58G[39mstill[64Gdoes[69Gits[73G50/50[79GRRF;[84Gthese[90Gare[94Gnew,[99Gseparate[108Gmodules[116Gyou[120Gcan[124Grun[128Gand[132Greason[139Gabout[145Gindependently.[160GWhen[165Gyou[169Gwant[174Gto[177Gdecide[184Gwhether[192Ganything[201Gbeyond[208Gvector[215Gbelongs[223Gin[226Gthe[230Gdefault[238Gpath,[244Gthe[248Ghonest[2C[1Btest is[11Glabelling real queries in [38;2;177;185;249meval/plexus_queries.jsonl[39m — not[69Ganother ratio.[84G[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCrunched for 3m 6s[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;8;145;178m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[48;2;8;145;178m[38;2;0;0;0m fix-embedder-re-embed-corpus [49m[38;2;8;145;178m──[1B[39m❯ What was the exact logic for keyword search in RDB? What I meant here with RDB is searching in Postgres with the given query. Exact matching does happen for certain keywords; for example, asking "help me make a financial plan for next quarter" will[K[1B  fo[K[61;1H[59;5H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[4C[58Bc[61;1H[59;6H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[5C[58Bu[61;1H