[2C[1B[22m[K[2C[1BSummary[11Gis[14Gsimply[21G[1mone more text poured into the same card, stamped B[22m:[2C[1B[K[2C[1Btitle  [22GA[29G[K[2C[1Bsummary  → s[16Gamped B      ← your[36Gnew field[2C[1Bbody[8G+[10Gintent/task_type/domain[34G→[36Gstamped[44GD[2C[1B[K[2C[1BTwo[7Gconsequences,[21Gboth[26Gvisible[34Gin[37Gthat[42Gexample:[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mIt adds vocabulary the prompt never uses.[45G[22m[38;2;177;185;249mdifficult[39m,[56G[38;2;177;185;249mdebrief[39m,[65G[38;2;177;185;249msubtext[73G[39mare[77Gin[80Gthe[84Gsummary[92Gbecause[100Gyou[104Gwrote[110Gthem[115Gthere.[122GThey[127Garen't[134Gin[137Gthe[141Gprompt's[150Ginstruction[162Gtext.[168GSomeone[176Gsearching[186G[3m"debrief a difficult meeting"[216G[23mnow[220Gmatches[228Gthis[233Gprompt[240G—[242Gbefore[2C[1Bsummaries,[14Gthey[19Gwouldn't[28Ghave.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mIt outranks body matches.[29G[22mA[31Gword[36Gfound[42Gin[45Gthe[49Gsummary[57Gis[60Gtagged[67GB[69Gand[73Gscores[80Ghigher[87Gthan[92Gthe[96Gsame[101Gword[106Gburied[113Gin[116Gthe[120Gbody[125Gat[128GD.[131GThat's[138Gwhat[143Gmakes[149Gthe[153Gsummary[161Gpunch[167Gabove[173Gits[177G~250[182Gcharacters.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BThat's the[14Gmechanism[24Gbehind[31Gthe[35Gthing[41GI[43Gmeasured[52Gearlier:[61Gstrip[67Gthe[71Gtitle[77G(weight[85GA)[88Gand[92Glexical[100Grecall[107Ghalves,[115Gbecause[123Gon[126Ga[128Gcorpus[135Gof[138G[3minstructions[23m,[152Gtitle[158Gand[162Gsummary[170Gare[174Gthe[178Gonly[183Gtext[188Gthat[193Gsays[198Gwhat[203Gthe[207Gprompt[214Gis[217G[1mfor[221G[22m—[223Gthe[227Gbody[232Gonly[237Gsays[242Ghow[246Git[2C[1B[1mbehaves[22m.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BOne no[10Ge:[13Gthis only applie[30G to the [1mkeyword[46G[22mhalf of[54Gy[56Gur se[62Grch.[67GThe vector half doesn't use [38;2;177;185;249msearch_tsv[39m at all; it u[119Ges the[126Gembeddings in [38;2;177;185;249mprompt_chunks[39m, and those are built from title + chunk text with[204Gno[207Gsummary[215Gin[218Gthem[223Gyet.[228GSo[231Gyour[236Gsummaries[246Gare[2C[1Bcurrently[13Ghelping[21Gkeyword[29Gsearch[36Gand[40Gdoing[46Gnothing[54Gfor[58Gsemantic[67Gsearch[74G—[76Gwhich[82Gis[85Gprobably[94Gthe[98Gbigger[105Gopportunity,[118Gsince[124Ga[126Gsummary[134Gdescribes[144Gintent[151Gin[154Gexactly[162Gthe[166Gway[170Gembeddings[181Gare[185Ggood[190Gat[193Gcapturing.[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GSautéed for 1m 1s · 1 shell still running[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m※[3G[1mrecap: [22m[3mYou're r[19Gworking capillarie[38G'[40Gr[42Gtrieval; the pipeline now runs chunk-level vector plus lexical union with Qwen3 embedding and reranking, and you're generating prompt summaries (510 of 1025 done). Next: finish summary generation, then add [2C[1Bsummaries to the chunk embeddings so semantic search benefits too.[1B[23m[39m[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mActual[10Gy[12Ghaving summaries helps both out bec[48Guse o[54G one hand[64GI can get specific keywords for[96Gcontext,[105Gsubjec[112G, tech[119Gstack, etc... to use search_tsv with. On the other hand summaries have inherently more context than just title while compressing from [1B[39m  [38;2;255;255;255mthe full body for convenience; some titles may sound good or fit semantically but not fit my specific tech stack or hard requirements[39m                                                                                                                       [1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mYou're[10Gright,[17Gand[21Gmy[24Gframing[32Gwas[36Gabout[42Ghow[46Git's[51Gcurrently[61Gwired[67Grather[74Gthan[79Gwhat[84Git[87Gcan[91Gdo.[95GThe[99Gtech-stack[110Gpoint[116Gis[119Gthe[123Gsharp[129Gone[133G—[135Ga[137Gtitle[143Gcan[147Gbe[150Gsemantica