[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2C[52B[38;2;233;154;122mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[52B[38;2;215;119;87m✽[3G[38;2;230;149;117mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2C[52B[38;2;225;139;107mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2C[52B[38;2;223;134;102mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2C[52B[38;2;220;129;97mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[52B[38;2;215;119;87m✻[3G[38;2;218;124;92mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[2C[52B[38;2;215;119;87mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[52B[38;2;215;119;87m✶[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[3G[K[2C[1BThose letters are the important part:[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B┌[21G┬[38G┬[74G┐[4C[1B [11Gtag[23G    me[31Gs[40G   [44G       [53Gsource[4C[2B[1mA[22m          [17G [19G [23Gmost important[44G[1mtitle[22m    [54G [56G   [60G        [69G    [2C[1B├[21G┼[38G┼[74G┤[2C[1B│[5G[1mB[21G[22m│[23Gimportant[38G│[40Gthe[44G[1msummary[74G[22m│[2C[1B├─────────────────┼────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤[K[2C[1B│[5G[3m(no letter)[17G[23m=[19GD[21G│[23Gordinary[38G│[40Gthe[44G[1mbody text[54G[22m+[56Gthe[60Gtaxonomy[69Gtags[74G│[2C[1B└─────────────────┴────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┘[K[2C[2BSo [38;2;177;185;249mmeet[39m is in both[22Gthe[26Gtitle[32Gand[36Gthe[40Gsummary.[49G[38;2;177;185;249m'busi':91[59G[39mhas[63Gno[66Gletter[73G—[75G[38;2;177;185;249mbusiness[84G[39mappears[92Gonly[97Gin[100Gthe[104Gbody.[110G[38;2;177;185;249m'difficult':5B[125G[39m—[127Gthat[132Gword[137Gexists[144G[3monly[149G[23min[152Gthe[156Gsummary;[165Gnowhere[173Gin[176Gthe[180Gtitle[186Gor[189Gbody.[2C[2BWhen Postgres ranks results, [38;2;177;185;249mts_rank_cd[39m scores an A-match well above a[74GD-match.[83GSame[88Gword,[94Gdifferent[104Gworth[110Gdepending[120Gon[123Gwhere[129Git[132Gcame[137Gfrom.[2C[2B[1mWhere summary fits[22G[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BSummary is simply [1mone more text poured into the same card, stamped B[22m:[2C[2Btitle    → stamped A[K[2C[1Bsummary[12G→[14Gstamped[22GB[29G←[31Gyour[36Gnew[40Gfield[2C[1Bbody + intent/task_type/domain → stamped D[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BTwo[7Gconsequences,[21Gboth[26Gvisible[34Gin[37Gthat[42Gexample:[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mIt adds vocabulary the prompt never uses.[45G[22m[38;2;177;185;249mdifficult[39m,[56G[38;2;177;185;249mdebrief[39m,[65G[38;2;177;185;249msubtext[73G[39mare[77Gin[80Gthe[84Gsummary[92Gbecause[100Gyou[104Gwrote[110Gthem[115Gthere.[122GThey[127Garen't[134Gin[137Gthe[141Gprompt's[150Ginstruction[162Gtext.[168GSomeone[176Gsearching[186G[3m"debrief a difficult meeting"[216G[23mnow[220Gmatches[228Gthis[233Gprompt[240G—[242Gbefore[2C[1Bsummaries,[14Gthey wouldn't have.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mIt outranks body matches.[29G[22mA[31Gword[36Gfound[42Gin[45Gthe[49Gsummary[57Gis[60Gtagged[67GB[69Gand[73Gscores[80Ghigher[87Gthan[92Gthe[96Gsame[101Gword[106Gburied[113Gin[116Gthe[120Gbody[125Gat[128GD.[131GThat's[138Gwhat[143Gmakes[149Gthe[153Gsummary[161Gpunch[167Gabove[173Gits[177G~250[182Gcharacters.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BThat's the mechanism behind the thing I measured earlier: str[65Gp[67Gthe title (weight[85GA) and lexical recall halves, because on[126Ga corpus of [3minstructions[23m, title and[162Gsummar[170Gare the only text th[193Gs[195Gys what the[207Gprompt[214Gis[217G[1mfor[221G[22m—[223Gthe[227Gbody[232Gonly[237Gsays[242Ghow[246Git[2C[1B[1mbehaves[22m.[1B[K[2C[1BOne[7Gnote:[13Gthis[18Gonly[23Gapplies[31Gto[34Gthe[38G[1mkeyword[46G[22mhalf[51Gof[54Gyour[59Gsearch.[67GThe[71Gvector[78Ghalf[83Gdoesn't[91Guse[95G[38;2;177;185;249msearch_tsv[106G[39mat[109Gall;[114Git[117Guses[122Gthe[126Gembeddings[137Gin[140G[38;2;177;185;249mprompt_chunks[39m,[155Gand[159Gthose[165Gare[169Gbuilt[175Gfrom[180Gtitle[186G+[188Gchunk[194Gtext[199Gwith[204Gno[207Gsummary[215Gin[218Gthem[223Gyet.[228GSo[231Gyour[236Gsummaries[246Gare[1B [3Gcurrently helping keyword search and doing nothing for semantic search — which is probably the bigger opportunity, since a summary describes intent in exactly the way embeddings are good at capturing.[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GSautéed for 1m 1s · 1 shell still running[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m※[39m [38;2;153;153;153m[1mrecap: [22m[3mYou're reworking capillaries' retrieval; the pipeline now runs chunk-level vector plus lexical union with Qwen3 embedding and reranking, and you're generating prompt summaries (510 of 1025 done). Next: finish summary generation, then add [23m[39m[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153m[3msummaries to the chunk embeddings so semantic search benefits too.[1B[23m[39m[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mActually having summaries helps both out because on one hand I can get specific keywords for context, subject, tech stack, etc... to use search_tsv with. On the other hand summaries have inherently more context than just title while compressing from [39m  [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mthe full body for convenience; some titles may sound good or fit semantically but not fit my specific tech stack or hard requirements[39m                                                                                                                       [1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mYou're right, and my framing was about how it's[51Gcurrently[61Gwired[67Grather[74Gthan[79Gwhat[84Git[87Gcan[91Gdo.[95GThe[99Gtech-stack[110Gpoint[116Gis[119Gthe[123Gsharp[129Gone[133G—[135Ga[137Gtitle[143Gcan[147Gbe[150Gsemantically[163Gperfect[171Gand